cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Refute, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Refute: find signals, try to kill them, keep what survives"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lucilla
    given-names: Klauber
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-4519-5457"
version: 0.4.0
date-released: 2026-11-03
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/klucilla/refute"
url: "https://github.com/klucilla/refute"
abstract: >
  Refute is an open-source framework where agents try to break scientific
  claims before anyone believes them. Claims are pre-registered and locked
  with SHA-256 hashes, attacked by deterministic falsification tests and a
  blind holdout, and reported in reproducible evidence dossiers.
keywords:
  - falsification
  - reproducibility
  - pre-registration
  - exoplanets
  - TESS
